#!RuleTest
#test CDISC-CG0218 expect=noViolation domain=SV
#runLevel Info
#note "A date-only visit on a transition date (2012-07-09 ends SCREENING and starts TREATMENT, SE Assumption 10) may have started before or after the transition instant, so which element was in progress at the start of the visit (SV Assumption 11) cannot be determined. PLAN-cg0218-transition-day-precision (B2, owner 2026-10-05): the visit is judged against both adjacent elements - SCREENING, which ends on the visit day with no time on either side, MAY still be in progress and is a candidate; TREATMENT contains the visit. EPOCH SCREENING matches a candidate, so nothing fires at ERROR or at INFO (and neither would TREATMENT, valid_transition_day). The PhUSE pilot data uses both conventions (SCREENING to TREATMENT: the starting element; TREATMENT to FOLLOW-UP: the ending one). History: option 1 (owner 2026-10-02) excluded such a visit from judgement altogether; the quantifier replaced the exclusion."
dataset SV label="Subject Visits"
col STUDYID type=Char label="Study Identifier"
col DOMAIN type=Char label="Domain Abbreviation"
col USUBJID type=Char label="Unique Subject Identifier"
col VISITNUM type=Num label="Visit Number"
col VISIT type=Char label="Visit Name"
col SVSTDTC type=Char label="Start Date/Time of Visit"
col EPOCH type=Char label="Epoch"
---
CDISCPILOT01 | SV | 01-701-0001 | 2 | DAY 1 | 2012-07-09 | SCREENING
---

dataset SE label="Subject Elements"
col STUDYID type=Char label="Study Identifier"
col DOMAIN type=Char label="Domain Abbreviation"
col USUBJID type=Char label="Unique Subject Identifier"
col SESEQ type=Num label="Sequence Number"
col SESTDTC type=Char label="Start Date/Time of Element"
col SEENDTC type=Char label="End Date/Time of Element"
col EPOCH type=Char label="Epoch"
---
CDISCPILOT01 | SE | 01-701-0001 | 1 | 2012-07-06 | 2012-07-09 | SCREENING
CDISCPILOT01 | SE | 01-701-0001 | 2 | 2012-07-09 | 2012-08-20 | TREATMENT
---
